# Functional upper blepharoplasty and blepharoptosis repair (15822, 15823, 67901-67908), from Medicare LCD L34411
# (Palmetto GBA). Status draft: awaiting clinical sign-off (vaglio signoff). Every clause is quoted from
# library/sources/L34411-blepharoplasty.txt; the codes are those of its billing and coding article A56503.
#
# Drafted by hand. Functional, and so covered, when the upper lid or overhanging skin produces a functional deficit of
# the visual field or brow fatigue, or for one of the other functional indications the LCD lists. Denied when it is
# done solely for cosmetic reasons, or when every indication is documented absent. The LCD lists dermatochalasis
# itself among the functional indications; it is kept as written, for the clinician to read with the rest. The LCD
# text read here gives no visual-field threshold or photograph requirement for these procedures; a plan's own rule for
# them belongs in its version. Not decided here: brow lift (67900), lower lid and other eyelid surgery. States: Palmetto's
# jurisdictions J and M; check the contractor's current list.
policy blepharoplasty
  title "Functional upper blepharoplasty or blepharoptosis repair (15822, 15823, 67901-67908)"
  version 0.1.0
  source "Medicare LCD L34411, Blepharoplasty, Eyelid Surgery, and Brow Lift (Palmetto GBA)"
  status draft
  authority lcd
  lines medicare-advantage medicare
  states AL GA TN NC SC VA WV
  questionnaire https://vaglio.example/Questionnaire/blepharoplasty
  service cpt 15822 15823 67901 67902 67903 67904 67906 67908

evidence visual_field_deficit
  text "The upper lid position or overhanging skin produces a functional deficit of the visual field, or brow fatigue"
  clause "Upper blepharoplasty (removal of upper eyelid skin) and/or repair of blepharoptosis (drooping of the upper eyelid, which relates to the position of the eyelid margin with respect to the eyeball and visual axis) is considered functional in nature when the upper lid position or overhanging skin (see “pseudoptosis” below) is sufficiently low to produce a functional deficit related to visual field impairment or brow fatigue."
  find question visual-field-deficit
  request document loinc 28570-0

evidence dermatochalasis
  text "Dermatochalasis: excess eyelid skin with loss of elasticity"
  clause "Dermatochalasis: excess skin with loss of elasticity that is usually the result of the aging process"
  find question dermatochalasis

evidence chronic_dermatitis
  text "Chronic dermatitis from blepharochalasis due to severe allergy or thyroid eye disease"
  clause "Chronic dermatitis due to blepharochalasis (excess skin associated with chronic recurrent eyelid edema that physically stretches the skin) due to severe allergy or thyroid eye disease"
  find question chronic-dermatitis

evidence spectacle_fitting
  text "Significant difficulty fitting spectacles because of excess eyelid tissue"
  clause "Significant/extreme difficulty fitting spectacles due to excessive eyelid tissue"
  find question spectacle-fitting

evidence blepharospasm
  text "Debilitating essential blepharospasm for which all other treatments failed or are contraindicated"
  clause "Primary essential idiopathic blepharospasm (uncontrollable spasms of the periorbital muscles) that is debilitating for which all other treatments have failed or are contraindicated"
  find question blepharospasm

evidence prosthesis_fitting
  text "An anophthalmic socket with ptosis making a prosthesis hard to fit"
  clause "Anophthalmic socket with ptosis contributing to difficulty fitting a prosthesis"
  find question prosthesis-fitting

evidence cosmetic_only
  text "Done solely for cosmetic reasons"
  clause "Surgeries performed solely for cosmetic reasons are not considered reasonable and necessary and therefore, not covered by Medicare."
  find question cosmetic-only

criterion no_indication
  text "No functional indication is documented."
  clause "Medicare considers surgeries performed to improve function as reasonable and necessary."
  defeated by visual_field_deficit dermatochalasis chronic_dermatitis spectacle_fitting blepharospasm prosthesis_fitting

criterion not_cosmetic_only
  text "It is not shown to be done solely for cosmetic reasons."
  clause "Surgeries performed solely for cosmetic reasons are not considered reasonable and necessary and therefore, not covered by Medicare."
  defeated by cosmetic_only

decision approve approves
  text "Approve the surgery as functional."
  clause "Medicare considers surgeries performed to improve function as reasonable and necessary."
  defeated by no_indication cosmetic_only

decision deny_no_indication denies
  text "Deny: no functional indication; the surgery is not shown to improve function."
  clause "Medicare considers surgeries performed to improve function as reasonable and necessary."
  defeated by visual_field_deficit dermatochalasis chronic_dermatitis spectacle_fitting blepharospasm prosthesis_fitting

decision deny_cosmetic denies
  text "Deny: done solely for cosmetic reasons."
  clause "Surgeries performed solely for cosmetic reasons are not considered reasonable and necessary and therefore, not covered by Medicare."
  defeated by not_cosmetic_only
